# grant.cm

Monorepo with two independent pnpm packages, orchestrated from the root `justfile`:

- `frontend/` — the Next.js (Pages Router) website. The main app.
- `scripts/` — Google Cloud utilities (Medium data sync, Google Doc → PDF resume sync). Deploy/automation tooling, not part of the website.

## Toolchain

- Node.js (see `.nvmrc`), pnpm `9.15.9` (pinned via `packageManager`), and `just` (task runner).

## Commands (run from repo root)

- Install: `just install`
- Dev server: `just dev` → http://localhost:3000
- Lint: `just lint` (autofix: `just fix`)
- Build: `just build`
- Run a scripts package script: `just scripts <script>`

## Conventions

- The dev server runs on port 3000; the production `start` script uses 8080.
- TypeScript throughout; code style is enforced by `gts` (Google TypeScript Style).
- `scripts/` needs Google Cloud credentials (`GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS`) to run against real services; not required for frontend development.
- Deploys: pushing to `main` deploys to Cloud Run via GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/deploy.yaml`).
- `next dev` auto-generates `frontend/AGENTS.md` and `frontend/CLAUDE.md`; these are gitignored — do not edit or commit them.

See the root `AGENTS.md` for the canonical, longer-form guidance.
